<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="51435" href="schedule/2020/spring/GLBL/296/51435.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2020" href="schedule/2020.xml">2020</calendarYear><term id="120201" href="schedule/2020/spring.xml">Spring 2020</term><subject id="GLBL" href="schedule/2020/spring/GLBL.xml">Global Studies</subject><course id="296" href="schedule/2020/spring/GLBL/296.xml">Global St Foundation Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Water, Hmn Rights &amp; Dev</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 16-Mar-20 - 06-May-20.</sectionDateRange><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Water scarcity is an essential feature of 21st century life. While here in Champaign we enjoy clean tap water from the pristine Mahomet Aquifer, crises around access and purity of water about in many parts of the US and the global South. In this course we will look at debates over water and water policy, examining crisis focal points like Flint Michigan and Cape Town, South Africa along with analyzing the dynamics of the privatization of water and grassroots movements to access clean water and sanitation.</sectionText><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2020-03-16Z</startDate><endDate>2020-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>03:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>M      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>145</roomNumber><meetingDateRange>Meets 16-Mar-20 - 06-May-20.</meetingDateRange><buildingName>Armory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Kilgore" firstName="J">Kilgore, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>